/*Instantiation of Objects in C++
-------------------------------------------------------------
1. Definition of Instantiation of Objects

Instantiation of an object is the process of creating an actual object (instance) of a class in memory. A class is only a blueprint or design, while an object is its real instance that can store data and use the functions defined by the class.

Hindi:
Object Instantiation का अर्थ है किसी class का actual object बनाना। Class एक blueprint या design की तरह होती है, जबकि object उस class का real instance होता है जो memory में space लेता है और class के data members तथा member functions को use कर सकता है।

Easy Example
Student s1;

यहाँ:

Student → Class

s1 → Object

Student s1; → Object Instantiation

Object बनने पर memory में उसके लिए space allocate होता है।

2. Class  vs Instantiation
Term	            Meaning
Class	            A blueprint or template for creating objects

Instantiation	    The process of creating an object from a class

Easy Understanding
Class
  ↓
Blueprint / Design
  ↓
Instantiation
  ↓
Object Created
  ↓
Memory Allocated

For example:

class Student
{
public:
    string name;
    int age;
};

3. Basic Program of Object Instantiation-:

#include <iostream>
using namespace std;
class Student
{
public:
    string name;
    int age;
    void display()
    {
        cout << "Name = " << name << endl;
        cout << "Age = " << age << endl;
    }
};
int main()
{
    // Object instantiation
    Student s1;
    s1.name = "Adil";
    s1.age = 22;
    s1.display();
    return 0;
}

Types of Object Instantiation in C++--------------------
--------------------------------------------------
The main ways of object instantiation/object creation in C++ can be explained as follows.

1. Static / Automatic Object Instantiation--:

Automatic object instantiation is the process of creating an object as a local variable. The object is automatically destroyed when its scope ends.Its lifetime is controlled by its scope.

Automatic object instantiation का अर्थ है object को local variable के रूप में create करना। जब object का scope समाप्त हो जाता है, तो object automatically destroy हो जाता है। इसका lifetime उसके scope द्वारा controlled होता है।

Example:
Student s1;

2. Multiple Object Instantiation--:

Multiple object instantiation is the process of creating two or more objects of the same class. Each object has its own separate set of non-static data members and can store different values.Multiple objects of the same class can exist at the same time.

Example:
Student s1;
Student s2;
Student s3;

3. Object Instantiation Using a Parameterized Constructor--:

Object instantiation using a parameterized constructor is the process of creating an object by passing specific arguments to a constructor so that the object can be initialized with the given values.The supplied arguments are passed to the parameterized constructor during object creation.

Example:
Student s1("Adil", 22);

4. Dynamic Object Instantiation--:

Dynamic object instantiation is the process of creating an object dynamically at runtime using the new operator. The allocated memory is released using delete.

Dynamic object instantiation का अर्थ है runtime पर new operator की सहायता से object create करना। इसकी dynamically allocated memory को delete द्वारा release किया जाता है।

Example:
Student *s1 = new Student;
To release the object:
delete s1;

5. Object Instantiation Using a Copy Constructor--:

Copy constructor instantiation is the process of creating a new object by copying the state or values of an existing object of the same class.

Copy constructor के द्वारा object instantiation का अर्थ है किसी existing object की values को copy करके नया object create करना।

Example:
Student s1;
Student s2 = s1;

Here, s2 is created by copying s1.

Key Point:
The copy constructor is automatically invoked when a new object is initialized from an existing object.

6. Object Instantiation Using Move Constructor

Move constructor instantiation is the process of creating a new object by transferring resources from a temporary or expiring object instead of copying them.

Move constructor के द्वारा object instantiation में temporary या expiring object के resources को copy करने के बजाय नए object में transfer किया जाता है।

Example:
Student s2 = std::move(s1);

7. Main Characteristics of Object Instantiation

1. Creates an Object — 

 Instantiation creates an actual object from a class.

 Instantiation class से actual object create करता है।

2. Memory Allocation — 

 When an object is created, memory is allocated for its non-static data members.

 Object create होने पर उसके non-static data members के लिए memory में space मिलता है।

3. Object Gets Its Own Data

 Each object normally has its own copy of non-static data members.

 प्रत्येक object के पास normally अपने non-static data members की अलग values होती हैं।

Example:

Student s1;
Student s2;

4. Member Functions Can Be Used

 An instantiated object can access the class's accessible member functions.

Object class के accessible member functions को call कर सकता है।

s1.display();

5. Constructor May Be Called Automatically

When an object is instantiated, the appropriate constructor is automatically called if one exists.

Hindi: Object instantiate होने पर appropriate constructor automatically call हो सकता है।

Student s1;

तो default constructor call हो सकता है।

6. Different Objects Can Have Different Values

Objects of the same class can contain different data values.

Hindi: एक ही class के अलग-अलग objects में अलग-अलग values हो सकती हैं।

s1 → Name = Adil
s2 → Name = Rahul
7. Object Has a Lifetime

An object exists for a specific lifetime determined by how and where it is created.

Hindi: Object का एक lifetime होता है, जो उसके creation के तरीके और scope/storage duration पर depend करता है।

8. Destructor May Be Called Automatically

When an automatic object reaches the end of its lifetime, its destructor is automatically called.

Hindi: Automatic object का lifetime समाप्त होने पर उसका destructor automatically call होता है।

Object Created
      ↓
Constructor
      ↓
Object Used
      ↓
Object Destroyed
      ↓
Destructor

8. Instantiation and Constructor Difference

 Instantiation                            Constructor                           
 ---------------------------------------  --------------------------------------
 Object creation की process है            Special member function है             
 Class से object create करता है            Object को initialize करता है           
 Example: `Student s1;`                  Example: `Student()`                   
 यह कोई function नहीं है                   यह एक special member function है       
 Object के creation को represent करता है  Creation के समय initialization करता है 


9. Instantiation and Destructor Relationship
Class
  ↓
Object Instantiation
  ↓
Object Created
  ↓
Constructor Called
  ↓
Object Used
  ↓
Object Lifetime Ends
  ↓
Destructor Called
  ↓
Object Destroyed

