Age = 20
Age = 25

5. Function Overloading

English:
Function overloading is a feature of C++ that allows multiple functions to have the same name but different parameter lists.

Hindi:
Function Overloading C++ का feature है जिसमें एक ही नाम के multiple functions बनाए जाते हैं, लेकिन उनके parameter list अलग होते हैं।

Syntax
void show(int a);
void show(int a, int b);
Example

#include <iostream>
using namespace std;
void show(int a)
{
    cout << "One parameter: " << a << endl;
}

void show(int a, int b)
{
    cout << "Two parameters: " << a + b << endl;
}

int main()
{
    show(10);
    show(10, 20);


    return 0;
}

One parameter: 10
Two parameters: 30

6. Default Parameter vs Function Overloading — Difference
| Basis                   | Default Parameter                         | Function Overloading                                      |
| ----------------------- | ----------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------- |
| **Meaning**             | Gives a predefined value to a parameter   | Creates multiple functions with the same name             |
| **Number of Functions** | Usually one function                      | Two or more functions                                     |
| **Parameter Value**     | Uses default value if argument is omitted | Selects a matching overloaded function                    |
| **Main Purpose**        | Provide optional arguments                | Perform different operations using the same function name |
| **Syntax**              | `void show(int x = 10);`                  | `void show(int x);` and `void show(int x, int y);`        |
| **Code**                | Usually less code                         | Requires multiple function definitions                    |
| **Flexibility**         | Allows optional arguments                 | Allows different parameter lists                          |
| **Ambiguity**           | Can cause ambiguity with overloads        | Can cause ambiguity when signatures overlap               |
| **Example Call**        | `show()` or `show(10)`                    | `show(10)` or `show(10,20)`                               |

⭐ Exam Difference

Default parameter provides an optional value to a parameter, whereas function overloading allows multiple functions with the same name but different parameter lists.

